# Card/spell art was migrated OUT of Git LFS (Jul 2026): the 2.9MB PNGs blew
# GitHub's 1GB/month LFS bandwidth on every Vercel redeploy, blanking all art.
# Now compressed WebP stored as normal git blobs — no LFS, no bandwidth limit.

# The generated roster is compared against a freshly rendered copy by
# roster.test.ts. Rendering always emits LF, so the file has to stay LF on
# disk too - under core.autocrlf=true a checkout would otherwise hand the
# test a CRLF copy and fail it for a reason unrelated to the cards.
docs/ROSTER.md text eol=lf
